      "rationale": "\ud83d\udc0d\ufe0f No third-party library in any ecosystem reads or writes `s.norm.en1994` \u2014 checked against PyPI, which serves no `en1994`, `eurocode`, `vdi3805` or `iso16757` distribution, and whose nearest real packages (`structuralcodes`, `concreteproperties`, `anastruct`) implement design-code formulae and speak no interchange format \u2014 so this subset's reference is a SECOND IMPLEMENTATION rather than a third-party distribution. That is why `package` is empty: the entry links no external library and contributes nothing to the dependency ratchet. The implementation is `../../../../../\ud83e\uddea\ufe0ftests/mutate-en1994-1/\ud83d\udc0d\ufe0fcomponent.py`, all 22 kinds of `En1994Mutation` written in Python from `26/08/12/SEMANTIC-MUTATIONS-OVERHAUL`'s `\ud83d\udcd3\ufe0ftaxonomy.md` (verb table, the `new_<field>` naming mechanic, the addressing convention) and `\ud83d\udcd3\ufe0fderivation-rules.md` (shape rules), plus this manifest's own catalog for the closed list of kinds. It imports nothing from the Rust it judges and transliterates none of it \u2014 the field a `new*` argument names is resolved by normalised spelling against the document's own keys, exactly as the naming mechanic states. Its reading is pinned by reaching every committed handcrafted `(before, mutation, after, outcome)` vector and by re-emitting the committed `.dsl.semio` artifact byte for byte, neither of which a misreading could do.\n\nUNDER PROTOCOL V2 this registration is classified `cross-semio-implementation` \u2014 a required SUPPLEMENTAL oracle that does not discharge `en1994-1-mutate`'s external-oracle requirement for its 22-kind mutation vocabulary; a qualifying third-party reference (`third-party-library` / `third-party-cli` / `standards-reference-tool`) is still owed.\n\n[2026-09-02, D1 \u2014 SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION] Promoted from cross-semio-implementation to verified-native-second-implementation: this artifact is semio-native (isSemioNativeArtifact), this reference's own third-party survey above (kept verbatim) already names what was checked and declined, its python implementation differs from the Rust subject, and it covers 100% of this manifest's 1 capability/capabilities with 22 committed fixture vector(s). See .\ud83e\uddecsemio/\ud83e\udd91\ufe0frepo/\ud83c\udfab\ufe0ftickets/\ud83c\udf86\ufe0f26/\ud83c\udf19\ufe0f09/\u2600\ufe0f02/SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION/\ud83d\udcd3\ufe0fd1-native-oracle-discharge.md.",
